This chapter follows the family of Robert Penhallow, Tamsin's grandfather, back to Cornwall. His grandfather, John Penhallow, was a tin miner from St Just who came to the Wisconsin lead district with his wife, Elizabeth Trembath, and settled at Mineral Point. Robert's wife, Joan, came from another Mineral Point family, the Treloars.

The story begins in Penwith, at the far western end of Cornwall. It then follows John and Elizabeth's son William to the farm at Dodgeville, and ends with Robert and Joan's household in Madison.

